            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0189" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg179"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.9111 RR/3–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-14">March 14,
                        1949</date>.<lb/>[Received March 14—5:22 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>870. <hi rendition="#italic">China Press</hi> March 14 carried Sun Fo statement
                    on arrival Shanghai from Nanking last Saturday<anchor n="2" xml:id="d213-f1"/>
                    that China should take neutral stand in event of third world war and be neither
                    anti-US nor anti-USSR. Sun predicted Communists would join Soviet bloc when in
                    control China. Also declared that China’s failure obtain satisfactory results
                    from past foreign policy due to deterioration in relations among wartime allies
                    which affected Chinese situation. According to Sun, China was not responsible
                    for this state of affairs, and there had been “no big mistakes in China’s
                    foreign policy”.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Nanking 516, Canton 155.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
